<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F002" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T20:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Command allowlist enforcement checks basename only, not binary identity — bypassable" ;
  triage:description "scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py defines `ALLOWED_CLIENT_BINARIES = {\"atm\", \"atm.exe\", \"atm-graft\", \"atm-graft.exe\"}` and `require_client_command()` checks membership via `Path(command[0]).name.lower()` — a basename-only check (confirmed at line 71-73). A PATH-shadowed or absolute-path attacker binary named \"atm\" (not the real atm binary) bypasses this allowlist entirely. This is exactly the attack shape BLOCKING-03's own original description named, so the fix is incomplete against its own stated threat model." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBQA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "arch-ctm reported (message re: dbe489db) that command identity is now anchored to ATM_SMOKE_INSTALL_ROOT/bin/<executable> when that env var is set, closing the basename-only bypass. Independently re-verified against feature/pAI-s27-peer-delivery-observability @ dbe489db: scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py::require_public_client_command (~lines 96-104) resolves the expected path from ATM_SMOKE_INSTALL_ROOT and rejects any command[0] that does not resolve to that exact path, falling back to shutil.which() only when the env var is unset. Ran python3 -m pytest scripts/smoke/test_run_peer_pair.py -q -- 5 passed, including the new test_validation_rejects_path_shadow_when_install_root_is_selected asserting a RuntimeError containing 'does not resolve' for a shadow binary. Full scripts/smoke/ suite (35 tests) also passed. Note: this closes the PATH-shadow/absolute-path bypass when ATM_SMOKE_INSTALL_ROOT is set (the harness's actual runtime mode); a caller that omits the env var still falls back to basename-only shutil.which() resolution, which is a narrower residual than the original finding but not a full elimination of basename trust in every code path." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s16/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s17/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s18/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s19/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s20/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s27/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F002/s27-fixed-dbe489db> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s27> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s27> .

